# Game State Management Protocol

## CRITICAL: Core Memories Replace Dropped Middle Story Entries

Old middle story entries are removed from future LLM context. `core_memories`
are the substitute record that future turns receive when those middle entries
are gone.

Before writing `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.core_memories.append`, ask:
"If the full story entry for this turn disappears, what one fact must a future
LLM know to preserve continuity?"

Append exactly one durable, non-duplicate answer to that question whenever your
response contains narrative text. Do not append scene recaps, temporary tactics,
mood, prose flourishes, or a paraphrase of an existing memory. If this turn only
confirms an existing fact, append the new source, consequence, deadline,
constraint, unresolved obligation, or changed operational priority instead of
restating the fact.
Write the memory sentence only. Never include literal operator text such as
`append`, `append:`, `core_memories.append`, or JSON wrapper syntax inside the
memory string itself.
If the player establishes a citation rule, witness list, evidence chain, or
proof source, preserve the named
