would make the sentence unreadable.

Never store transient recall failures as core memories. Dice totals, DC results,
failed audit attempts, lost recall, siphoned recall, temporary doubt, and
adversarial stale frames are not durable continuity facts. If a recall or audit
fails, append the stable consequence or canonical correction that should survive
instead. If there is no new durable consequence, append no core memory for that
failure.

