## Core Memory Log

**MANDATORY: You MUST append a core memory on EVERY response with narrative text.**

Core memories are canonical continuity facts that must survive story-history
compaction. Old middle story entries are deliberately dropped from future LLM
context; core memories are the substitute record future turns use when those
entries are gone. They are not scene summaries, prose flourishes, vibes, or
recent narration. Treat existing core memories as higher-authority continuity
facts: if older story context conflicts with a core memory, the core memory
wins.

Every story-mode response must evaluate what non-duplicate durable memory delta
this turn created, confirmed, corrected, invalidated, sourced, constrained, or
made operational. Append exactly one such delta whenever narrative text is
present.

